-- title:
--   Lower-level 𝔪-torsion from a non-zero abelian-quotient coordinate
-- statement:
--   Fix a non-zero natural number $N_0$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, and a valuation subring $A$ of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$ lying over $p$, in the sense that the image of $p$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be a level-$N_0$ datum over $A$: a structure morphism $\Lambda.\sigma_A$ from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathbb Q$ at $p$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme $\Lambda.X$ with a morphism $\Lambda.f$ to that base, a relative group law on it, and bijections $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ from $\mathrm{JZero}\,N_0$ onto the sections over the generic point and $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ from $\mathrm{JZeroC}$ over the residue field of $A$ onto the sections over the residual point; assume $\Lambda.\mathrm{IsJacobian}$, i.e. $\Lambda.f$ carries the abelian-scheme property bundle, its group law is commutative, $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ is additive and Galois-equivariant, $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ is additive, reduction of points agrees modulo the maximal ideal whenever the mod-$\ell$ reduction inputs hold, and every element of the Hecke algebra $\mathbb T = \mathbb Z[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ is realised by an endomorphism of $\Lambda.f$ respecting the group law. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data: a smooth, separated, surjective group object $O.g$ over the same base with commutative relative group law, a bijection $O.\mathrm{pts}$ from $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0p)$ onto its generic sections which is additive, Galois-equivariant and intertwines the $\mathbb T$-action with endomorphisms of $O.g$, flat surjective multiplication-by-$n$ maps, preconnected fibres, proper generic fibre, and the further fields of that structure. Assume the Hecke inputs and commutation of the bar Hecke operators at levels $N_0p$ and $N_0$. Let $\mathfrak m$ be an ideal of $\mathbb T$ containing $p$, and let $x \in \mathrm{JZero}(N_0p)$ lie in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,p$, the subgroup generated by the $p$-torsion points whose associated generic section extends over $\operatorname{Spec} A$; assume both degeneracy pushforwards $\mathrm{degeneracyPushforwardPair}\,N_0\,p\,i$ ($i = 0,1$) kill $x$, and that $x$ is $\mathfrak m$-torsion for the level-$N_0p$ Hecke module structure. Let $s$ be a section of $O.g$ over $\Lambda.\sigma_A$ with $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ equal to the generic point followed by $s$, and suppose that at least one of the two elements $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}(\mathrm{fibreMap}\,(O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i)\,(\text{residual point followed by } s))$, $i = 0,1$, is non-zero. Then $\mathrm{HasLowerLevelTorsion}$ holds for the set of prime factors of $N_0p$, the ideal $\mathfrak m$ and $\mathrm{JZero}\,N_0$ with its level-$N_0$ Hecke module structure: there is $y \in \mathrm{JZero}\,N_0$ with $y \ne 0$ such that $n \cdot y = 0$ for every natural number $n$ whose image lies in $\mathfrak m$, and $(X_\ell - b) \cdot y = 0$ for every prime $\ell$ not dividing $N_0p$ and every integer $b$ with $X_\ell - b \in \mathfrak m$.
--
--   This is Ribet's transport of $\mathfrak m$-torsion from the finite part of the $p$-torsion of the semistable level-$N_0p$ Jacobian down to level $N_0$, through the two abelian-quotient coordinates of the special fibre; it is the step in Mazur's principle where non-vanishing of one coordinate produces an $\mathfrak m$-torsion class of level $N_0$ with eigenvalue conditions away from the primes of $N_0p$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.hasLowerLevelTorsion_of_mem_finPts_of_not_mem_toricPts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.hasLowerLevelTorsion_of_mem_finPts_of_not_mem_toricPts), which supplies such a point by ruling out the toric alternative.
